  "final_answer_preview": "According to Section 314 of the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, 2023, if a person takes property belonging to another out of their possession, believing in good faith that the property belongs to themselves, they are not guilty of theft. This illustrates that the intention behind the act is crucial in determining whether theft has occurred. For instance, if A takes property from Z, genuinely believing it to be A's own, A does not commit theft at that moment. However, if A later discovers the mistake and dishonestly keeps the property, A may then be guilty of dishonest misappropriation.",
